<h2>What Happens If the Knicks Win Game 5</h2>
<p>Game 5 is Saturday, June 13 in San Antonio. The Knicks need one win. If they close the series, Brunson will become the shortest Finals MVP winner since the award was formalized — and one of the physically least imposing stars ever to win a championship as the primary engine.</p>
<p>The physical measurements will not change. His wingspan will still be 1,679th out of 1,812 tested. His height will still be 1,617th. What will change is the data point at the top of his page: NBA champion. The combine did not predict that. It never measures the things that produce it.</p>
